  "established_semantics": [
    {
      "finding": "The published ptap1/ntap1 simulation model is an ohmic resistor driven by R; it does not use W/L and does not accept A/P as device-model inputs. The diode extractor is a geometrical extraction mechanism, not evidence of a junction-diode simulation model.",
      "source": "ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/resistors_mod.lib",
      "lines": [
        19,
        35
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "Xschem computes A=W*L and P=2*(W+L) for LVS; simulation R follows area and perimeter conductances in parallel. PCell code uses the same expression and draws an Activ rectangle at W,L.",
      "source": "ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/xschem/sg13g2_pr/ptap1.sym",
      "lines": [
        18,
        27
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding": "All 64 tap records in the exact original I/O CDL use W=L. All Perim values equal 2*(W+L); published R values reproduce the square calculation within 0.01764 percent (printed rounding). This establishes square schematic metadata, but not why those square sides were selected or whether an arbitrary-shape equivalent was qualified.",
      "source": "exact original c4 I/O CDL plus analysis.json"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The strict reader uses explicit A and Perim values and correct SI-to-um scaling; ordered TIE/WELL and A/P are enabled. The parallel combiner sums both A and P. No unit or Perim-alias bug remains in this path.",
      "source": "custom_reader.lvs:643-647, custom_devices.lvs:179-201, custom_combiner.lvs:209-225"
    }
  ],
